        <interface show_pages="true" page_rows="2" page_width="788" page_height="528">
            <simulation_delay>0.1</simulation_delay>
            <isee:process_frame x="22" y="387" width="214" height="110" name="Asgnmnt_Backlog" show_name="false" color="#0CA0FF" border-style="solid" border-width="thin">
                <doc>This represents the number of assignments you are behind.  The teacher gives one new assignment daily.  The number of assignments you complete is based upon how much time you study each day, and how long it takes to complete each assignment.&#x0D;</doc>
            </isee:process_frame>
            <isee:process_frame x="279" y="537" width="212" height="110" name="GPA_1" show_name="false" color="#0CA0FF" border-style="solid" border-width="thin">
                <doc>Your GPA is based upon the number of assignments you have completed and the number of points you have gotten for each.  You are not penalized for incomplete work.  (You always can try to do it later).&#x0D;&#x0D;The purple line is your desired GPA.  The green line is your actual GPA.   The graph above shows the points you get for each assignment.  (As opposed to the cumulative GPA graphed here).</doc>
            </isee:process_frame>
            <isee:process_frame x="21" y="30" width="518" height="331" name="INTRO" show_name="false" color="#1D1D1D" border-style="solid" border-width="5px">
                <image width="426" height="325">data:image/png;base64,</image>
                <doc>Daily Study Time (DST) is the amount of time you spend each night on homework.  The Time Per Assignment (TPA) is the amount of time you take to complete each assignment. &#x0D;&#x0D;This means that if DST is 4 hours and TPA is 2 hours, you will complete 2 assignments every night.  On the other hand, if DST is 2 hours, and TPA is 4 hours, it will take two nights per assignment!&#x0D;&#x0D;Try these strategies for the first half of the simulation (20 weeks).  Then try to recover with good grades and no backlog!&#x0D;&#x0D;Peter Punt:     DST: 0.5 hour     TPA: 0.5 hour&#x0D;Larry Later:    DST: 0.5 hour     TPA: 4 hours&#x0D;Nancy Nerd:    DST: 4 hours      TPA: 4 hours </doc>
            </isee:process_frame>
            <isee:bundled_connector color="red">
                <from>INTRO</from>
                <to>Asgnmnt_Backlog</to>
                <pts>
                    <pt x="543" y="355" />
                    <pt x="22" y="355" />
                    <pt x="22" y="365" />
                </pts>
            </isee:bundled_connector>
            <isee:bundled_connector color="red">
                <from>GPA_1</from>
                <to>Energy</to>
                <pts>
                    <pt x="279" y="591" />
                    <pt x="236" y="591" />
                </pts>
            </isee:bundled_connector>
            <isee:process_frame x="26" y="536" width="211" height="109" name="Energy" show_name="false" color="#0CA0FF" border-style="solid" border-width="thin">
                <doc>This is the amount of personal energy that you have.  Too much time spent studying will cause it to decline.  If you lower your time studying, your energy will gradually regenerate.&#x0D;</doc>
            </isee:process_frame>
